.TH "GLESHA-STATE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-state \- migrate local state out of the config directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha state migrate [GLOBAL OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Moves older post-clean-slate state from the platform config directory's
glesha/state-v2 directory to the current state directory. No cloud requests are made.
Stop other glesha processes first. Existing custom state locations remain supported.
.PP
Archives are moved without copying; source and destination must share a filesystem.
Pending work and identities are preserved. Original databases are retained under
.state-migration-backup in the destination. Repeat the command after interruption.
An existing destination or unsupported database is refused. Config and credentials
are never moved or rewritten.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
Use TOML settings. catalog.directory overrides the migration destination.
.TP
.B \-\-env FILE
Accepted as a global option; migration does not load credentials.
.TP
.B \-L, \-\-log-level LEVEL
debug, info, warn, error or silent. Default: info.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
yes, no or auto. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and build revision.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B Linux
$XDG_DATA_HOME/glesha/state, or ~/.local/share/glesha/state.
.TP
.B macOS
~/Library/Application Support/glesha/state.
.TP
.B Windows
%LOCALAPPDATA%\eglesha\estate.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha state migrate
glesha state migrate --config /path/to/config.toml
glesha help state migrate
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
glesha(1), glesha-cleanup(1)
